@meta
id: 23-06
title: A closed fold is one line
chapter: 23
type: lesson
skills: folds
par: 30
minutes: 5
vscode: click the chevron in the gutter, then select and delete
open: order.provider.ts

@brief
`legacyRefund` has been dead since the payment service was rewritten.
Remove the whole method and the blank line after it, so `cancel` is
followed directly by `ship`.

It is a trap for the tools you have. `dap` stops at the blank line in
the middle of the method. `d%` from the brace is characterwise and
leaves the signature behind. Counting lines for `dd` is how you end up
off by one.

Fold the method first. A fold is a range of lines vim displays as one,
and — this is the useful part — every linewise command treats a closed
fold as a single line.

@keys
| `zf{motion}` | create a fold over the lines the motion covers |
| `zo` `zc` | open, close the fold under the cursor |
| `za` | toggle it |
| `zd` | delete the fold (the text stays) |
| `dd` `yy` `>>` on a closed fold | act on every line inside it |

@hints
`/legacyRefund` puts you on the signature. `$` puts you on its opening
brace, and `%` is the matching close brace.
--
`zf%` from the brace folds the whole method into one line. `zo` to
check it is the right one, `zc` to close it again.
--
With the fold closed, `dd` deletes the whole method. One more `dd`
takes the blank line it leaves behind.

@solution
    /legacyRefund<Enter> $zf% dd dd :wq<Enter>

Twenty-six keystrokes and no counting.

`zf` is an operator like `d` or `y`: it takes a motion or a text
object and folds those lines. `zf%` from a brace is the reliable way to
fold a method or block, because `%` does not care about blank lines
inside it. `zfap` folds a paragraph, `zfip` the same without the
trailing blank, `zf3j` four lines.

A fold you have created is closed, and a closed fold is one line to
`dd`, `yy`, `p`, `>>`, `J`, `j` and `k`. That is what makes folds an
editing tool rather than just a display setting. Yank a closed fold
and paste it somewhere else: the whole block moves. Press `j` over a
closed fold: you skip it.

`zo` opens, `zc` closes, `za` toggles. `zd` removes the fold itself
and leaves the text. Manual folds vanish when you close the file;
the next two lessons show vim building them for you.

@start order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }

  public async cancel(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }

    await this.paymentService.refund(order.id);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }

  public async legacyRefund(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status !== 'CANCELLED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_CANCELLED');
    }

    const receipt = await this.paymentService.refundLegacy(order.id, order.total);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { refundReceipt: receipt.id },
    });
  }

  public async ship(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'SHIPPED' },
    });
  }
}

@expected order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }

  public async cancel(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }

    await this.paymentService.refund(order.id);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }

  public async ship(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'SHIPPED' },
    });
  }
}
